(:id "port/python/packet/fixed-arrays" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/python/python_packet_arrays_test.go: TestPythonPacketArrays" "internal/codegen/python/python_packet_arrays_test.go: TestPythonPacketArraysNegativeControl" "make python-packet-arrays-negative-control (make/python.mk)") :tested-revision "e751f0cfad60da908d94f62891c4273e798c436e" :note "2026-11-15: fixed arrays [N]T of bool, bare and ranged integers, enums, flags, types and unions, at the top level, inside an if branch and inside union arms: the fixture's values write byte-identical to the Go leg's writer and read Go's bytes back to the same value, the probecollider C++ pin reads and writes back byte-identical, a wrong length, a non-list and a bad element are refused with InvalidValue at the element's path, every truncation and a trailing byte are Refused and every single-bit flip is Refused or reads a value that writes back, and the generated package is mypy --strict clean; the negative control edits a copy of the generated reader and goes red by name. Run on Linux x86_64 with the pinned CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2 (make dist-python), SCHEMA_SLOW=1, at this revision.")
(:id "port/python/packet/counted-arrays" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/python/python_packet_arrays_test.go: TestPythonPacketArrays" "internal/codegen/python/python_packet_arrays_test.go: TestPythonPacketArraysNegativeControl" "make python-packet-arrays-negative-control (make/python.mk)") :tested-revision "e751f0cfad60da908d94f62891c4273e798c436e" :note "2026-11-15: counted arrays [..N]T and [A..B]T of the same element kinds: the count rides offset from its minimum (a hand-checked vector, 01 02 1d 20 00), the fixture's values write byte-identical to the Go leg's writer and read back to the same value, a counted array is born at its minimum and reads as empty in an untaken branch, a length outside [A, B] is refused with InvalidValue, a count above its bound is Refused on read; the negative control reads the count from 0 instead of its minimum in a copy of the generated reader and goes red on the vector by name. Run on Linux x86_64 with the pinned CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2 (make dist-python), SCHEMA_SLOW=1, at this revision.")
